From 87e1c7f603ef7a2f02c6f6b9cf3caa0ab25512b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritvik Rao <rsrao2@illinois.edu>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:40:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Bucketed GVT: --gvt-node-waves combines each process's
 count-wave contributions in shared memory

Each PE writes its wave contribution (counts, buckets passed, controller
counters and histogram) as one flat array into its process's slot; the last
PE in combines the slots and the process contributes once, through a custom
reducer instead of a tuple. The result comes back once per process (a
nodegroup broadcast) and each PE runs it from execute(), so no PE handles
22 contributions or 22 result copies per wave. Optimistic scheduler only,
off under --sched-park. check_counts is split so both paths share
wave_done(). Tests: six *_nodewaves configs (108/108, 1080/1080 with
--repeat 20 at 2x2, 2x4, 1x8); existing bucketed configs 504/504.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
